## Why This Is Asked
Tests spanning multi-tenant boundaries and asynchronous export flows surface data isolation and resilience issues. This question probes end-to-end coverage for real-world SaaS data export use cases like Airbnb and Microsoft enterprise products.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data isolation across services
- Async background jobs and eventual consistency
- End-to-end validation of blob storage and email delivery
- Idempotent retries and fault injection
- Test data strategy and environment isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test outline (Playwright + API stubs)
test('tenant-scoped data export end-to-end', async ({ page, api, storage }) => {
  await loginAsAdmin(page);
  await page.click('#start-export');
  await page.waitForResponse(r => r.url.includes('/exports/').and(r.status() === 200));
  const status = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
  const blob = await storage.getBlob(`exports/${tenantId}/data.json`);
  expect(blob).toContain(`"tenantId":"${tenantId}"`);
  // idempotence
  await page.click('#start-export');
  const status2 = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status2).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you parameterize test data for tenants with different data shapes?
- How would you enforce data privacy in the test environment while validating exports?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a privacy-critical, cross-service E2E flow—data erasure across region boundaries, backups, and auditability. It probes data isolation, idempotency, and outage resilience in a realistic multi-service setup.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-by-design data deletion across microservices
- Cross-region data isolation and leakage prevention
- Idempotent delete semantics
- Deterministic testing via ETL mocks
- End-to-end audit trails and backup purge checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold for Cypress/Playwright
describe('Delete My Data E2E', () => {
  it('erases tenant data across services and purges backups on SLA', async () => {
    await loginAsUser('regionA');
    await triggerDeleteRequest();
    await verifyServiceDeletion('Auth');
    await verifyServiceDeletion('CRM');
    await verifyServiceDeletion('Analytics');
    await verifyServicePurgeBackups();
    // idempotency
    await triggerDeleteRequest();
    await verifyNoOp(),
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical thinking about multi-tenant security, performance, and rollout discipline in E2E tests, which are common in large SaaS platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and data bleed prevention
- Canary rollout and per-tenant feature flags
- Per-tenant UI customization and data caches
- End-to-end data drift, latency, and observability

## Code Example

